+# National Archives control numbers for FAA directive and signature-authority files
+
+November 9, 2026 Eastern · B129 / PD01–PD04. The rendered National Archives Catalog identifies a **46-carton FAA directives series**, local ID **OK-5A**, arranged by year and FAA file classification number. The description includes drafts, issued directives and clearance records. Two accession numbers and nine records-center transfer numbers give more precise ways to locate a 1985 folder inventory. The specific file for **FAA Order 1360.16**, the corrected answer and the FAA’s signed decision remain unacquired. [Directives series](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/2723191) · [Prior accession comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/2bf8d4d845d5a0c6feaa59794c7397a6674510b7/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-directive-case-file-accessions-2026-11-09/README.md)
+
+## Directives case files
+
+- **Series description.** NAID **2723191** identifies the Mike Monroney Aeronautical Center, Management Analysis Division, as creator. The catalog describes draft and final directives with supporting records for issue, revision or cancellation. Its arrangement section groups the records by year and then by FAA file classification number. The title and **Collected** field give **1979–1995**. The **Covers** field gives **1978–1994**. Preserve both date fields. [Catalog series description and arrangement](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/2723191)
+- **Archived copy.** The record identifies Kansas City as the archived-copy location, with paper extent **45 linear feet, 11 linear inches**. The Copy 1 details show **46 FRC Carton, Standard**. The catalog labels the series **Access: Unrestricted**, **Use: Unrestricted** and **Not Yet Available Online**. It cautions that the archived-copy location may differ from current availability. The location and count are catalog observations. [Catalog copy and availability fields](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/2723191)
+- **Control numbers.** The rendered accession list gives **NRFA-2009-237-0007** and **NRFA-2009-237-0010**. The expanded records-center transfer list gives **237-04-0025**, **237-92-0015**, **237-93-0013**, **237-94-0064**, **237-94-0074**, **237-96-0025**, **237-97-0065**, **237-98-0042** and **237-98-0049**. The earlier College Park accession **LTI-0237-2016-0027** has a similar title, date field **1/1/1979-2/28/1995** and count **1 container**. Keep those fields separate from the Kansas City catalog’s fields. A folder list or transfer manifest with both identifiers would test whether the College Park container relates to the cataloged series. [Catalog control numbers](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/2723191) · [College Park accession listing](https://www.archives.gov/research/accessions/2016-quarter-2)
+
+## Separate signature-authority series
+
+The 2022 relocation list calls **NAID 241990398** *Organizational Planning Files*. The rendered catalog title is **Organizational Planning Files Signature Authority, 2006–2008**. It identifies the FAA **Southwest Region, Program Evaluation Office**, local ID **237-SW10B**, and a Kansas City paper copy. Copy 1 details give **1 linear foot, .3 linear inch** and **1 FRC Carton, Standard**. The series is marked **Not Yet Available Online**. The full catalog title gives a more specific lead for regional delegation records. The relation, if any, to the headquarters decision and the governing 2006 authority remains open. [Relocation list](https://www.archives.gov/fort-worth/2022-fortworth-records-move) · [Rendered signature-authority record](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/241990398)
+
+## Access observations and discriminating records
+
+The earlier web retrievals reported **Cache miss**, and both direct HTTP requests yielded identical **5,454-byte** HTML bodies with empty app roots. This session obtained the rendered public catalog descriptions and copy controls at the same two addresses. The observations describe different retrieval surfaces and times. Their separate captures and digests are preserved. An exact-title catalog search for **"FAA Correspondence Manual"** displayed no results. Its scope was one search of the public catalog, with the series pages available separately by identifier. Item-level indexing and folder contents remain unverified. [Search result](https://catalog.archives.gov/search?page=1&q=%22FAA%20Correspondence%20Manual%22) · [Capture hashes and verified locators](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+For the manual, the next discriminating input is a box or folder inventory under **2723191 / OK-5A** keyed to **1985** and the applicable FAA classification, checked against **1360.16**, **July 12, 1985** and historical office **APF-100**. An exact folder match would support examining the issued text, clearances, amendments and distribution. A separate accession-to-series crosswalk would test the relationship to the College Park container. For 2006, identify the office named in the actual decision before assigning the regional signature-authority file any case relevance. The corrected answer, delivery acknowledgment, signed action or no-action decision, OIG recommendation outcomes and case-specific policy routing remain TODOs. [FAA manual locator](https://www.faa.gov/documentLibrary/media/Order/0000.5E.pdf#page=14) · [OIG recommendations, pp. 12–13](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf#page=12)
+
+Verification covered five saved browser accessibility snapshots, 41 anchor checks and two rehashed predecessor HTML sources. Source pins give the capture timestamp, UTF-8 byte counts, SHA-256 values and exact snapshot line locators. The hash scope is the saved rendered text. The research originals retain the full captures locally. [Source pins](SOURCE-PINS.json) · [Text addition](TEXT-CHANGES.diff)
